  "rationale": "Every exfiltrate_* technique needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold there plus stolen_dbadmin, and stolen_dbadmin needs admin_ciserver, admin_dc or admin_adfs. The ciserver route is the shortest: (1) phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, (2) pivot_internal gives reach_internal (no segmentation), (3) auth_ciserver, (4) escalate_ciserver (unpatched), (5) leak_secrets_ciserver gives stolen_dbadmin, (6) auth_db, (7) escalate_db, (8) exfiltrate_db. The DC/ADFS route needs extra steps (auth_appserver, kerberoast, auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc) and totals 10. No step in the 8-step chain can be skipped, because each one supplies a precondition that nothing cheaper provides."
